                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00068         * Function table. Please note, that on entry to these subroutines, the main temp stack is already
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00069         * allocated (33 bytes), B=# of parameters received
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00070         * Sneaky trick for end of table markers - it does a 16 bit load to get the offset to the function
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00071         *  routine. It has been purposely made so that every one of these offsets >255, so we only need a
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00072         *  single $00 byte as the high byte to designate the end of a table
