                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00397         *   X = pointer to "stkdepth" byte scratch variable area (same as stack pointer, which has allocated that extra memory)
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00398         *   U = pointer to 2nd parameter (first parameter after name itself)
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00399         *   D = # of parameters (NOTE: function name itself is always parameter 1)
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00400         
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00401         * Stack on entry to every function routine (with stkdepth set to 9):
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00402         *   $00-$08 / 00-08,s - temporary scratch variable area
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00403         *   $09-$0A / 09-10,s - RTS address to BASIC09/RUNB
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00404         *   $0B-$0C / 11-12,s - # of parameters (including function name itself)
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00405         *   $0D-$0E / 13-14,s - pointer to 1st parameter's data (function name)
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00406         *   $0F-$10 / 15-16,s - length of first parameter
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00407         * From here on is optional, depending on the function being called, there can be up to 9 parameter pairs
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00408         * (pointer/value and length).
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00409         * The temporary stack uses 0,s as the path #, and 1,s + as the output buffer.
                      (/basic09/gfx2.asm):00410         
